      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For international travel with potential transit through multiple countries, focus on the \"transit\" vs. \"entry\" distinction. Always check the specific immigration website for each connecting country to confirm if the layover duration requires exiting the airport's international transit zone. Since you are connecting between Singapore, Malaysia, and onward to Vietnam/Thailand, verify if these stops require a formal visa even for short layovers. Consulting the official government immigration site for each specific location is the safest way to prevent delays.",
      "source": "target",
